  "courseSlug": "mastering-linux",
  "courseTitle": "Mastering Linux: The Comprehensive Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38501198",
      "title": "Setup: VM with Multiple Storage Drives",
      "lectureOrder": 270,
      "videoOrder": 239,
      "sourceHash": "c20053cdb28133622a31d31b9e8425c7915420327a6127de300ea7fba8064597",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.23,
          "end": 5.24,
          "en": "In this chapter, we want to have a look at how we can prepare the virtual machine for this chapter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.24,
          "end": 11.93,
          "en": "We need to add the following drives to our VM three times a drive with 50GB of size and one time a drive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 11.93,
          "end": 14.21,
          "en": "with 150GB of size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.24,
          "end": 17.48,
          "en": "Don't worry, we will not write that much data to the disk.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.48,
          "end": 22.28,
          "en": "So even if on your host, on your computer, you don't have that much storage, don't worry about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.28,
          "end": 23.96,
          "en": "You can still follow along.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.96,
          "end": 29.12,
          "en": "It will not occupy this much space on your hard drive after this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.12,
          "end": 34.37,
          "en": "Once we have done this, we might have to install LVM on our computer on ubuntu.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 34.4,
          "end": 36.77,
          "en": "That would be an apt install lvm2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.77,
          "end": 44.78,
          "en": "And on centos that might be a DNF install lvm2 though at least in my installation of CentOS LVM has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 44.78,
          "end": 47.39,
          "en": "been configured already and it's already in use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 47.39,
          "end": 50.66,
          "en": "So in my case on ubuntu I have to install it on centos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 50.66,
          "end": 51.35,
          "en": "I don't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 52.76,
          "end": 53.93,
          "en": "So here I am.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.93,
          "end": 58.79,
          "en": "This is my VirtualBox and I will now add the following drives I go into the settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.97,
          "end": 62.78,
          "en": "One thing I want to note be sure that the virtual machine is powered off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 63.11,
          "end": 66.02,
          "en": "There are ways, for example, also to pause a virtual machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 66.02,
          "end": 73.49,
          "en": "In that case you have to unpause it or resume it and then just shut it down normally and it should really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 73.49,
          "end": 74.6,
          "en": "be powered off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 74.63,
          "end": 78.02,
          "en": "Now, once it's powered off, we can go into the storage here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 78.02,
          "end": 80.84,
          "en": "And now I want to add another storage drive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 80.87,
          "end": 86.96000000000001,
          "en": "I do this by selecting the controller and now I can add a new hard disk here, and I want to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 86.96000000000001,
          "end": 88.33,
          "en": "a new hard drive now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 88.88,
          "end": 90.35,
          "en": "Oh, I don't need to click add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 90.35,
          "end": 93.86,
          "en": "I need to create a new hard drive as a file format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 93.86,
          "end": 94.85,
          "en": "VDI is all right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.85,
          "end": 95.99000000000001,
          "en": "That's from VirtualBox.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.99000000000001,
          "end": 97.03999999999999,
          "en": "I click next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.82,
          "end": 103.58,
          "en": "We should definitely not preallocate the spare space that would improve the performance, but we will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.58,
          "end": 106.43,
          "en": "not store that much data on our drives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.43,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "So the actual amount of data that you need on your host computer is significantly less than 300GB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 117.3,
          "en": "It's maybe one gigabyte maximum unless you click that one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 117.3,
          "end": 120.42,
          "en": "If you click that one, then you will need the full 300GB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.42,
          "end": 122.67,
          "en": "So I would recommend you not to click that one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.67,
          "end": 126.72,
          "en": "And now the first drive should be 50GB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 126.72,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "Then I click finish here and this is now the drive that I would like to connect to my virtual machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 133.74,
          "en": "So I will now click Choose here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.74,
          "end": 140.1,
          "en": "And now this drive here has been added the same thing I now need to do two more times with a size of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 140.1,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "50GB, so I need to create yet another drive with the size of 50GB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 146.61,
          "end": 149.19,
          "en": "Click finish here and click Choose here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 149.19,
          "end": 150.84,
          "en": "So this is now my second drive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 150.87,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "Then I do exactly the same thing again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 153.75,
          "en": "Create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 153.78,
          "end": 154.35,
          "en": "Next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.38,
          "end": 155.19,
          "en": "Next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.82999999999998,
          "end": 157.03,
          "en": "50GB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.03,
          "end": 158.17000000000002,
          "en": "Finish, choose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.17000000000002,
          "end": 164.68,
          "en": "So now we have our three drives and later in the chapter we will need one more drive with 150GB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.68,
          "end": 172.75,
          "en": "So what I'll do is I will create next, next 150GB and click finish and click choose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.75,
          "end": 176.05,
          "en": "So now we have here our boot drive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 176.07999999999998,
          "end": 181.51,
          "en": "This is what we'll be booting from Those are the three drives that we will use at the beginning of the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.51,
          "end": 182.02,
          "en": "chapter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.02,
          "end": 187.48,
          "en": "And then later we will also use this one with 150GB in physical terms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.48,
          "end": 193.12,
          "en": "That would mean we would have one hard disk or SSD with 25GB that we boot from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 193.12,
          "end": 198.76,
          "en": "Right now, it may be a different size for you, but then we have this will be the one, the first drive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 198.76,
          "end": 205.93,
          "en": "We will be working on one additional physical drive with 50GB, another physical drive with 50GB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 205.96,
          "end": 213.13,
          "en": "Again, another drive with 50GB again and one SSD or HDD with 150GB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 213.13,
          "end": 216.82999999999998,
          "en": "So that's why we need those for additional drives here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 216.82999999999998,
          "end": 219.38,
          "en": "Once we are done, we can just click okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 219.38,
          "end": 221.72,
          "en": "And now the settings are saved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 222.35,
          "end": 227.45,
          "en": "Now we can just boot up and now we will have additional drives attached to our system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 227.69,
          "end": 233.6,
          "en": "Last but not least, I need to make sure that LVM is installed, but that can be solved with a simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 233.6,
          "end": 234.56,
          "en": "apt install.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 235.43,
          "en": "Lvm2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 235.46,
          "end": 236.81,
          "en": "Let's just have a look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 236.81,
          "end": 241.94,
          "en": "If it's installed here and here, in my case it's already installed, but in your case most likely on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 241.94,
          "end": 245.58,
          "en": "ubuntu, it will need to download and install that tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 245.6,
          "end": 248.72,
          "en": "It's installed here because I have installed it before already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 249.08,
          "end": 255.26,
          "en": "So now everything is prepared and we can now start to have a look at LVM and how LVM works and what's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 255.26,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "the structure there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 256.22,
          "end": 258.59,
          "en": "We'll have a look at that in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
